node_modules/
dist/
.sidecrew/
*.tsbuildinfo
.stryker-tmp/
reports/
.sidecrew-mutation/
.build/
.swiftpm/
# Muter copies the package to a sibling <name>_mutated/ and writes muter_logs/, and cleans up neither.
# The verifier removes both; a `muter run` by hand in the fixture does not.
muter_logs/
*_mutated/
.DS_Store
# Editor state. Not ours to carry, and # Agent worktrees. Checkouts of this repo, so committing them would nest the repo in itself.
.claude/worktrees/
.idea/ in particular records local absolute paths.
.idea/
.vscode/

# ── client code never enters git ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The workload-#2a experiments run against real client projects, and three kinds of artefact quote
# those projects **verbatim**: the rendered prompt (the files as they are on disk), the worker's answer
# (the whole file back), and the review pack (a unified diff of both). The measurements — funnel
# counts, S, A, latencies, the ADRs — contain none of it, and those are the parts worth keeping.
#
# `.gitignore` only stops a file being added; it does not remove one already committed, and a push
# sends the whole history regardless. See docs/DECISIONS.md ADR-0051.
experiments/go-no-go-2a/c3/*/prompts/
experiments/go-no-go-2a/c3/*/answers/
experiments/go-no-go-2a/c3/*/tasks/
experiments/go-no-go-2a/review/*-pack.md
experiments/go-no-go-2a/results/coverage-*/
experiments/go-no-go-2a/results/overnight.log
# Change plans point at an absolute path into a client checkout and their asks quote the client's own
# symbol names (FULL_WARRANTY_TYPE_CODE, CENSORED_FIELDS). CLAUDE.md #7: local paths stay local, and a
# plan that quotes a client project is never committed. They live on disk; the results that reference
# them carry the numbers, which are ours.
experiments/go-no-go-2a/plans/
# Same rule for the planner-cost plans: §2.1's measurement plans a real client subtree, so the plan
# holds an absolute path into their checkout and its asks quote their own symbol names. The number the
# plan produces is ours and is committed; the plan is not.
experiments/planner-cost/plans/
# And §2.2's, for the same reason: an absolute path into a client checkout, and asks that name
# their files.
experiments/correction-round/plans/
# A replay saves whole verdicts so a disagreement can be diagnosed, and a verdict names the tests that
# regressed and quotes the compiler's words about the client's code. The result JSON beside them carries
# the counts, the hashes and D — which are ours (CLAUDE.md #7, ADR-0051).
experiments/gate-error-rate/results/*-verdicts/
# Same rule as every other run log here: a harness prints sandbox paths, and a sandbox is a copy of a
# client checkout. The measured result JSON beside it is written deliberately, carries counts and no
# identifiers, and IS committed.
experiments/gate-error-rate/results/*.log
# The fixture is our own code, so its handshake is safe and stays in the repo.
!experiments/go-no-go-2a/c3/fixture/prompts/
!experiments/go-no-go-2a/c3/fixture/answers/
!experiments/go-no-go-2a/c3/fixture/tasks/
!experiments/go-no-go-2a/review/fixture-pack.md

# Phase 11b arms quote the client's source by construction — a diff of their code is their code.
# Only the measurements (counts, tokens, verdicts) are ours to commit. CLAUDE.md #7, ADR-0051.
experiments/status-quo/arms/
experiments/status-quo/review/*-pack.md
# A run log prints the run id, which is built from the project directory's name.
experiments/status-quo/results/*.log

# python bytecode from the experiment scripts
scripts/__pycache__/

# Phase 14b's probe logs and its `fix --report` dump. `fix` prints sandbox paths and a run id built
# from the project directory's name, so both carry the client into a file that looks like a number
# (HANDOFF § Standing hazards; caught twice during Phase 12). The measured result JSON beside them is
# written deliberately, with the run id stripped, and IS committed.
experiments/editing-ceiling/results/*.log
experiments/editing-ceiling/results/*-report.json

# Phase 14b probe 2 plans the same 30 tasks with narrowed asks, so it carries the same absolute path
# into a client checkout that the correction-round plans do. Same rule, same reason.
experiments/editing-ceiling/plans/

# Phase 14c: the refused set names files in a client tree. Its sha256 is in the committed census; the
# list itself is only ever local (CLAUDE.md #7).
experiments/reach/local/
experiments/reach/plans/
# The run log prints sandbox paths and a run id built from the project directory name.
experiments/reach/results/*.log
experiments/reach/results/*-report.json
# The working checkout's fingerprints: hashes plus its HEAD, which is only a commit id but is local state.
experiments/reach/results/watch-*.txt

# ADR-0082 D: workload #1 plans against a client module quote its code, and the exemplars are tests of
# it. The population list names client files. All local; the counts and hashes are committed.
experiments/test-first/plans/
experiments/test-first/local/
experiments/test-first/results/*.log
experiments/test-first/results/*-validate.json
experiments/test-first/results/*.txt
experiments/test-first/results/*-run.json
